       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline in adults, which is 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and agitation. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nPlease check which of these fits:\n\n1. **Typo or unit error.** You may have meant 40 mg or 200 mg. Typical dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrates up to 200 mg.\n2. **Intentional dose.** If it's deliberate, for example a specialist-directed regimen, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I can enter it flagged for pharmacy review.\n3. **Different drug or frequency.** The order may have been meant for something else.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
